From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: defcom5-rockchip <286489597+defcom5-rockchip@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:27:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_h4: rate-limit "Frame reassembly failed"

h4_recv() logs one line for every byte run the H4 state machine cannot
parse.  When a UART controller is power-cycled under a live hci device
(the AP6275P's BT_REG_ON is switched by the platform rfkill, so a desktop
"Bluetooth off/on" resets the chip, which comes back without its firmware
at its default 115200 baud while the host still talks at 1.5 Mbaud), every
byte the chip sends is garbage and the error is logged at line rate
until the open attempt times out:

  Bluetooth: hci0: Frame reassembly failed (-84)   x 426,378 in ~15 s

Measured on an Orange Pi 5B, one such event (413,270 lines in 23 s) left
the 200 MB persistent journal (SystemMaxUse=200M) at 198.8 MB with nothing
older than the first 24 s of that boot still retained, and journald
repeatedly reported "Missed N kernel messages".  The line carries no
information after the first few; use the rate-limited variant so a
misbehaving UART cannot flood the log.  hci_bcm.c, hci_qca.c and the other
UART protocols have the same line but were not exercised here.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_h4.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_h4.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_h4.c
index 1d0cdf023243..34ab1f5f9c91 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_h4.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_h4.c
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@ static int h4_recv(struct hci_uart *hu, const void *data, int count)
 				 h4_recv_pkts, ARRAY_SIZE(h4_recv_pkts));
 	if (IS_ERR(h4->rx_skb)) {
 		int err = PTR_ERR(h4->rx_skb);
-		bt_dev_err(hu->hdev, "Frame reassembly failed (%d)", err);
+		bt_dev_err_ratelimited(hu->hdev, "Frame reassembly failed (%d)", err);
 		h4->rx_skb = NULL;
 		return err;
 	}
